          "evidence": "Trusted Isolette forms show one source DataPort legally fanning out through separate binary PortConnections, and show Thread-local state, initialization, compute cases, and In(state). Publishing PART-09 pre-state independently of PART-10's returning directive breaks the apparent cycle; PART-11/PART-13 can similarly derive same-evaluation fail-closed outputs while updating only owner-local post-state.",
          "requested_change": "Use one root and Process actuationFeedback port, one root/Process segment, and two distinct Process/Thread fan-out segments for INT-12 and INT-19. Publish PART-09 demand context from In(demandPhase), and use In(recoveryPhase)/In(commandPhase) in PART-11/PART-13 guards; add no scheduler assumption or state owner."
        },
